## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical mastery of multi-layer caching, invalidation patterns, and race-condition handling under high load. It probes Redis and Memcached integration, Lua-based locks, and cross-region TTL coherence.

## Key Concepts
- Cache invalidation strategies across layers
- Redis pub/sub and keyspace notifications
- Per-key mutex with Lua scripting to prevent stampedes
- Write-through vs write-behind coherence
- Multi-region TTL synchronization

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: acquire per-key lock, fetch fresh data, set both caches
function getFeed(key) {
  if (Redis.get(key)) return Redis.get(key)
  if (Memcache.add(key + ':lock', 1, 1)) {
    const fresh = loadFromDB(key)
    Redis.set(key, fresh, 300)
    Memcache.set(key, fresh, 300)
    Memcache.delete(key + ':lock')
    return fresh
  } else {
    // wait and retry
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test stampede under simulated burst?
- How would you evolve this for cross-region replication?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable, globally distributed telemetry store with practical sharding, replication, and failover strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Two-level sharding (region then device_id)
- Multi-region replication with bounded staleness
- Online shard rebalancing without downtime
- Read-after-write guarantees in local region
- Regional failover and cross-region replay trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
// shard key resolver
function shardKey(region, deviceId, shardsPerRegion){
  const key = region + '|' + deviceId;
  let h = 0; for (let i = 0; i < key.length; i++) { h = (h * 31 + key.charCodeAt(i)) >>> 0; }
  return h % shardsPerRegion;
}
```

```javascript
async function writeEvent(event){
  const shard = shardKey(event.region, event.deviceId, regionConfig[event.region].shards);
  await writeToShard(event, shard, {consistency: 'quorum'});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would clock skew across regions affect bounds on staleness?
- What metrics would you use to verify online rebalancing safety and latency budgets?

